---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout title="Carlos Limón Ledesma | Software Architect">
  <header class="site-header">
    <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 flex items-center justify-between h-20">
      <a href="#top" class="brand-mark" aria-label="Carlos Limón Ledesma home">
        <span class="brand-mark__dot"></span>
        <span>CLL<span class="text-brand-400">.</span></span>
      </a>
      <nav class="hidden md:flex items-center gap-7 text-sm text-surface-400" aria-label="Main navigation">
        <a href="#impact" class="nav-link">Impact</a>
        <a href="#expertise" class="nav-link">Expertise</a>
        <a href="#experience" class="nav-link">Experience</a>
        <a href="mailto:carloslimonledesma@gmail.com" class="nav-cta">Let's talk <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
      </nav>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main id="top">
    <section class="hero-section max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6" aria-labelledby="hero-heading">
      <div class="hero-grid-pattern" aria-hidden="true"></div>
      <div class="hero-copy">
        <p class="eyebrow"><span class="status-dot"></span> Software Architect · Automotive Systems</p>
        <h1 id="hero-heading">Building dependable systems for <span class="gradient-text">high-stakes software.</span></h1>
        <p class="hero-lede">I turn complex product requirements into clear architecture, disciplined delivery systems, and production-ready C++ software.</p>
        <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 items-center mt-9">
          <a href="#experience" class="btn-primary">Explore my work <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a>
          <a href="mailto:carloslimonledesma@gmail.com" class="btn-secondary">Get in touch <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-meta"><span>Based in Querétaro, Mexico</span><span class="meta-divider"></span><span>Open to senior architecture conversations</span></div>
      </div>
      <aside class="hero-visual" aria-label="Calileus engineering identity">
        <div class="hero-visual__frame">
          <img src="/profile.jpg" alt="Calileus illustrated engineering identity" />
          <div class="hero-visual__scanline" aria-hidden="true"></div>
          <div class="hero-visual__label hero-visual__label--top">CALILEUS / SYSTEMS LAB</div>
          <div class="hero-visual__label hero-visual__label--bottom"><span class="status-dot"></span> BUILDING WITH INTENT</div>
        </div>
        <div class="hero-visual__caption"><span>Personal mark</span><strong>Code · Honor · Legacy</strong></div>
      </aside>
    </section>

    <section id="impact" class="section-band max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6" aria-labelledby="impact-heading">
      <div class="section-intro"><p class="eyebrow">01 / OUTCOMES</p><h2 id="impact-heading">Engineering judgment, measured.</h2><p>Senior engineering is making the right tradeoffs visible. These are the outcomes I use to evaluate whether a system and a team are getting better.</p></div>
      <div class="impact-grid">
        <div class="impact-item impact-item--featured"><strong>60<span>%</span></strong><span>less review effort through automated quality gates</span></div>
        <div class="impact-item"><strong>58<span>+</span></strong><span>software releases delivered</span></div>
        <div class="impact-item"><strong>14</strong><span>engineers led across a multidisciplinary product team</span></div>
        <div class="impact-item"><strong>80<span>%</span></strong><span>smaller delivery package after legacy refactoring</span></div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="expertise" class="section-band max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6" aria-labelledby="expertise-heading">
      <div class="section-intro"><p class="eyebrow">02 / CAPABILITIES</p><h2 id="expertise-heading">From architecture intent to working software.</h2><p>A pragmatic technical range grounded in modern C++, quality engineering, and the operating systems that make delivery repeatable.</p></div>
      <div class="capability-grid">
        <article class="capability-card"><span class="capability-number">01</span><h3>Architecture & design</h3><p>Component boundaries, event-driven systems, object processing pipelines, API design, and cross-platform decomposition.</p><div class="tag-row"><span>C++20</span><span>Distributed systems</span><span>Protobuf</span></div></article>
        <article class="capability-card"><span class="capability-number">02</span><h3>Quality as a system</h3><p>MISRA C/C++, static analysis, review standards, test strategy, and automated gates that protect engineering focus.</p><div class="tag-row"><span>GoogleTest</span><span>clang-format</span><span>CI quality gates</span></div></article>
        <article class="capability-card"><span class="capability-number">03</span><h3>Delivery leadership</h3><p>Repository governance, release models, technical direction, mentoring, and the communication between product and engineering.</p><div class="tag-row"><span>GitHub Actions</span><span>CMake</span><span>Linux / Windows</span></div></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section id="experience" class="section-band max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6" aria-labelledby="experience-heading">
      <div class="section-intro"><p class="eyebrow">03 / EXPERIENCE</p><h2 id="experience-heading">Ownership that spans the whole lifecycle.</h2></div>
      <div class="experience-list">
        <article class="experience-item experience-item--current"><div class="experience-date">APR 2022 — PRESENT</div><div><div class="experience-role"><h3>Software Architect & Lead Developer</h3><span class="experience-current">CURRENT</span></div><p class="experience-company">AUMOVIO / Continental Autonomous Mobility</p><ul><li>Own architecture, package definition, repository governance, integration, and release quality for Automotive Radar Logic Model products.</li><li>Lead a 14-person team through quotation, planning, implementation, validation, customer integration, and production deployment.</li><li>Designed the detection, tracking, classification, and customer object-list processing pipeline with protobuf and FMI simulation integrations.</li></ul></div></article>
        <article class="experience-item"><div class="experience-date">2015 — 2022</div><div><h3>University Professor & Facilitator</h3><p class="experience-company">Polytechnic University of Querétaro / Autonomous University of Querétaro</p><ul><li>Taught C/C++, mathematics, and formal logic while mentoring the next generation of technical problem-solvers.</li><li>Built automated grading and contest-management software, and managed examination content for the Mexican Logic Olympiad.</li></ul></div></article>
        <article class="experience-item"><div class="experience-date">2014 — 2016</div><div><h3>Software Development Consultant</h3><p class="experience-company">REXAM · IMPULSE TELECOM · Sancorzep Group · REGULES</p><ul><li>Delivered enterprise software for asset inventory and operations, carrying solutions from requirements through deployment, training, and maintenance.</li></ul></div></article>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="section-band max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6" aria-labelledby="projects-heading">
      <div class="section-intro"><p class="eyebrow">04 / SELECTED WORK</p><h2 id="projects-heading">A public record of engineering standards.</h2><p>Open-source work that makes the way I think about maintainability, collaboration, and design review tangible.</p></div>
      <div class="project-grid">
        <a href="https://github.com/ObsidianHonorCoders/ohc-template-repo" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="project-card"><div class="project-top"><span class="project-type">ENGINEERING TEMPLATE</span><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div><h3>ohc-template-repo</h3><p>A reusable C++ foundation with Dev Containers, CMake, GoogleTest, documentation, and automated quality controls.</p><span class="project-link">View repository</span></a>
        <a href="https://github.com/ObsidianHonorCoders/inheritance-chess" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="project-card"><div class="project-top"><span class="project-type">C++20 SYSTEM</span><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div><h3>inheritance-chess</h3><p>A modular chess engine exploring polymorphism, component-based architecture, event-driven design, and cross-platform testing.</p><span class="project-link">View repository</span></a>
        <a href="https://github.com/ObsidianHonorCoders" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="project-card"><div class="project-top"><span class="project-type">COMMUNITY</span><span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></div><h3>Obsidian Honor Coders</h3><p>An engineering community focused on modern C++, software quality, and collaborative development practices.</p><span class="project-link">Explore the organization</span></a>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="closing-section max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6" aria-labelledby="contact-heading">
      <div class="closing-panel"><p class="eyebrow">05 / CONTACT</p><h2 id="contact-heading">Good systems start with a good conversation.</h2><p>For architecture leadership, modern C++, or engineering excellence, I would be glad to compare notes.</p><div class="flex flex-wrap gap-4 mt-8"><a href="mailto:carloslimonledesma@gmail.com" class="btn-primary">Email Carlos <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/calileus" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="btn-secondary">LinkedIn <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a href="https://github.com/Calileus" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" class="btn-secondary">GitHub <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div>
    </section>
  </main>

  <footer class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-6 py-8 footer-line"><span>© {new Date().getFullYear()} Carlos Limón Ledesma</span><span>Built with Astro · Deployed on GitHub Pages</span></footer>
</Layout>
